1. Susceptibility-Separation-Phantom
   https://github.com/neuropoly/Susceptibility-Separation-Phantom
   Copyright (c) 2024 NeuroPoly
   Licensed under the MIT License.

   The chi-separation model in qsm_forward/qsm_forward.py (paramagnetic /
   diamagnetic susceptibility splitting, per-tissue chi+/chi- reference values,
   white-matter susceptibility anisotropy, the T2/R2, Dr, R2' and 3T-scaling
   maps, and the chi-sep-aware GRE signal model) is a Python port of this
   phantom. The per-tissue chi+/chi- values (CHISEP_TISSUE_PARAMS) and the
   white-matter anisotropy values (WM_ANISOTROPY_PARAMS /
   WM_TRACT_ANISOTROPY_PARAMS) are taken from the phantom's
   data/chimodel/SusceptibilityValues.mat and README Tables 1-2.

   Please cite:
     Ridani, S., De Leener, B., & Alonso-Ortiz, E. (2026). A realistic
     in-silico brain phantom for quantifying susceptibility anisotropy-induced
     error in susceptibility separation. bioRxiv.
     https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.04.07.716972

